# Job 17: config-time decisions in set_headers and compression (branch
# perf/http-config-precompute, not pushed; B is master d50d12c26 plus
# patches/http-config-precompute.diff, the four commits of that branch).
# Workload static1k-hdrs: the static1k share plus three constant
# "response_headers", compression off.  oha sends the Accept-Encoding of a
# browser on every request.
# NEEDS the runner patch jobs/17-runner-ae-workload.patch (the AE key and the
# static1k-hdrs workload); without it perf-job.sh refuses the WORKLOAD.
# Callgrind on the reference bench host (fixed request count, 1300 minus 300 requests, one
# keep-alive connection) counted the router per request: master 18368.5,
# B 16847.0 (-8.3%).  Without Accept-Encoding and headers (plain static1k)
# the count was 15035.1 against 14797.3 (-1.6%), under the lab band.
JOB=17-http-config-precompute
REV_A=d50d12c26fd390d92542ecc69cdc9e0aca7b1ba9
REV_B=d50d12c26fd390d92542ecc69cdc9e0aca7b1ba9
PATCH_B=patches/http-config-precompute.diff
WORKLOAD=static1k-hdrs
AE=gzip, deflate, br, zstd
CONNS=6
WARM=2
DUR=8
REPS=4
PERF=1
PRIMARY=r_instructions
EXPECT=r_instructions lower in B by 6 to 10 percent (callgrind: 8.3 percent); s_instructions follows; ok equal, bad 0, alerts 0
FALSIFY=r_instructions NO CLAIM, NOISY or a drop under 5 percent: the counted saving does not reach the oha path (check that the header arrives: a response to "identity;q=0" must be 406 in A and B)
